## Stage 1 — Java's Six-Month Release Cadence — Understanding the Version Landscape

- For thirteen years, Java had slow, multi-year release cycles.
- Java 7 launched in 2011; Java 8 in 2014; Java 9 in 2017.
- Each release bundled years of work and introduced massive migration risk.
- In 2017, Oracle switched to a six-month release cadence : a new Java version every March and September.

*Applies **jvm-internals-and-garbage-collection** to the decision above.*

