## Stage 2 — The Three Eras of Modern Java — What Each One Solved

- Java 8 to Java 25 covers eleven years and three distinct architectural shifts.
- Each era solves a specific category of pain that was previously handled by boilerplate, convention, or workarounds.
- The dedicated posts below go deep on each era with full before/after code pairs, internals, and migration guides.
- Era 1 (Java 8–11): Lambdas, Streams, and the LTS Baseline Java 8 ended the anonymous-inner-class era.

