## Stage 5 — The Real Migration Costs — Thread Pinning, Framework Lag, and Immutability Constraints

- Modernising a Java codebase is not cost-free.
- Understanding the real friction points prevents premature optimism in migration planning.
- Thread pinning is a hidden tax.
- Legacy JDBC drivers (Oracle thin driver before 23c, some MySQL drivers before 8.2), older connection pools (DBCP2, c3p0), and hand-written synchronized cache implementations can all pin virtual threads.

